WEBVTT

00:22:57.167 --> 00:23:00.268
So my reader research
on trust repair says that,

00:23:00.292 --> 00:23:02.893
"Number one, an apology
seems to be less important

00:23:02.917 --> 00:23:04.768
than an expression of responsibility."

00:23:04.792 --> 00:23:06.059
EP: Absolutely.

00:23:06.083 --> 00:23:07.393
AG: Saying, "I'm sorry,"

00:23:07.417 --> 00:23:09.768
showing that I feel remorse,
is nice emotionally.

00:23:09.792 --> 00:23:11.601
It doesn't convince you necessarily

00:23:11.625 --> 00:23:14.226
that I accept the harm
that I've done to you.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:17.108
And also that I'm going to
change my behavior moving forward.

00:23:17.132 --> 00:23:19.059
And so I always look for someone to say,

00:23:19.083 --> 00:23:23.434
"Look, whether I feel
that what I did was wrong,

00:23:23.458 --> 00:23:26.559
I recognize that I hurt you,
I take responsibility for that.

00:23:26.583 --> 00:23:28.726
And now I'm also going
to take responsibility

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:32.268
for adjusting in the following ways
to make sure it doesn't happen again."